#!/bin/sh
# Nothing to do after an upgrade (F58; SPEC design section 2). The account was kept or created by pre_upgrade. The hooks of systemd and
# dbus, which pacman runs after this script, do the rest on the paths this package ships: 30-systemd-daemon-reload-system (daemon-reload),
# dbus-reload (bus reload), 25-systemd-catalog (journal catalog). Repeating a call here would run it twice, and before the hook. The unit is
# never enabled or started here (zz-custodio-restart.hook restarts a running one): D-Bus activation and its socket start it. Nothing here touches the state directory. See docs/decisions/packaging.md.
# The socket of the Firefox snap (F173) is enabled and restarted. This script runs before the daemon-reload hook, so a changed socket
# unit is read at the next restart of the socket, not by this one.
systemctl enable custodio-firefox.socket || true
systemctl restart custodio-firefox.socket || true
:
